    "ls|LS16_S6_U_403": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 403 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 1ST  DECEMBER, 2015/AGRAHAYANA 10, 1937 (SAKA) \n \nCASTE BASED CENSUS \n \n403. SHRI ASHWINI KUMAR: \nSHRI GODSE HEMANT TUKARAM: \nSHRIMATI KOTHAPALLI GEETHA: \nADV. JOICE GEORGE : \n  \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has conducted caste/religion based census \nin the country; \n \n(b) if so, the details and objective thereof along with the total \npopulation/persons belonging to SC, ST and OBC separately in the country, \nState-wise; \n \n(c) the time by which the census data is likely to be released; \n \n(d)  whether the population of SC, ST and OBC has shown a declining \ntrend; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor, State-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HARIBHAI PARATHIBHAI CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a): Yes Madam;  a  Socio Economic and Caste Census (SECC) has been \nconducted in  the country.   \n(b) & (c) : As per the decision of Union Cabinet, a Socio Economic and \nCaste Census (SECC), 2011 is being carried out in all the States/Union \nTerritories of India with the financial and technical \n \n \n \n...2/- \n \n\n-2- \nLS US Q.No.403 FOR 01.12.2015 \n \nsupport of the Government of India. The Ministry of Rural Development \n(MoRD) and the Ministry of Housing & Urban Poverty Alleviation (MoHUPA) \nare the nodal Ministries in the Government of India for this combined \nexercise in rural and urban areas respectively. The office of the Registrar \nGeneral & Census Commissioner, India is rendering logistic and technical \nsupport. \n As on date, the SECC -2011 field enumeration is complete. The \nGovernment has constituted the Expert Group under the Chairmanship of \nShri Arvind Panagariya, Vice -Chairperson,  NITI AAYOG to cl assify the \nCaste names returned in SECC-2011.  \n \n(d) & (e): A statement showing Population and Growth Rate of Scheduled \nCastes and Scheduled Tribes by residence as per Census 1991, 2001 & \n2011 is given at Annex.  Data on OBC is not collected in Census of India. \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nANNEX TO LSUQ No. 403 for 01.12.2015 \nScheduled Castes Growth Rate as per Census  1991,2001 & 2011  \nS.No Name of the States/UTs Scheduled Castes Population  Growth Rate  \n2011 2001 1991 2011-2001 2001-1991 \n00 INDIA@ 201378372 166635700 138223277 20.85 20.56 \n01 JAMMU & KASHMIR* 924991 770155 N.A. 20.10 - \n02 HIMACHAL PRADESH 1729252 1502170 1310296 15.12 14.64 \n03 PUNJAB 8860179 7028723 5742528 26.06 22.40 \n04 CHANDIGARH 199086 157597 105977 26.33 48.71 \n05 UTTARAKHAND 1892516 1517186 1232316 24.74 23.12 \n06 HARYANA 5113615 4091110 3250933 24.99 25.84 \n07 NCT OF DELHI 2812309 2343255 1794836 20.02 30.56 \n08 RAJASTHAN 12221593 9694462 7607820 26.07 27.43 \n09 UTTAR PRADESH 41357608 35148377 28044139 17.67 25.33 \n10 BIHAR 16567325 13048608 9982448 26.97 30.72 \n11 SIKKIM 28275 27165 24084 4.09 12.79 \n12 ARUNACHAL PRADESH NSC 6188 4052 - 52.71 \n13 NAGALAND NSC NSC NSC - - \n14 MANIPUR 97328 60037 37105 62.11 61.80 \n15 MIZORAM 1218 272 691 347.79 -60.64 \n16 TRIPURA 654918 555724 451116 17.85 23.19 \n17 MEGHALAYA 17355 11139 9072 55.80 22.78 \n18 ASSAM 2231321 1825949 1659412 22.20 10.04 \n19 WEST BENGAL 21463270 18452555 16080611 16.32 14.75 \n20 JHARKHAND 3985644 3189320 2589252 24.97 23.18 \n21 ODISHA 7188463 6082063 5129314 18.19 18.57 \n22 CHHATTISGARH 3274269 2418722 2148358 35.37 12.58 \n23 MADHYA PRADESH 11342320 9155177 7478321 23.89 22.42 \n24 GUJARAT 4074447 3592715 3060358 13.41 17.40 \n25 DAMAN & DIU 6124 4838 3891 26.58 24.34 \n26 DADRA & NAGAR HAVELI 6186 4104 2730 50.73 50.33 \n27 MAHARASHTRA 13275898 9881656 8757842 34.35 12.83 \n28 ANDHRA PRADESH 13878078 12339496 10592066 12.47 16.50 \n29 KARNATAKA 10474992 8563930 7369279 22.32 16.21 \n30 GOA 25449 23791 24364 6.97 -2.35 \n31 LAKSH