    "ls|LS16_S6_U_475": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.475 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2015 \n \nSAUDI DIPLOMAT CASE  \n \n475.  SHRIMATI KOTHAPALLI GEETHA:  \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Gove rnment is aware of the diplomatic troubles \nmounted for India recently over the case of a Saudi diplomat \naccused of allegedly torturing an d raping two Nepalese \nwomen at his home in Gurgaon; \n \n(b)   if so, the facts thereof; and \n \n(c)  whether the Government h as framed certain new rules to \navoid such incidents in future and if so, the details thereof?  \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a)  Yes.  \n \n(b) The alleged rape case of Nepalese housemaids by  a Saudi \ndiplomat has been taken up with the Government of the Kingdom of \nSaudi Arabia through the established diplomatic channels. The \nmatter is under investigation by the Indian Law Enforcement \nAgencies.  Any further action will have to await the results  of the \ninvestigation. \n \n(c) The Vienna Convention on Diplomatic Relations 1961 deals \nwith the immunity and privileges granted to foreign diplomats for \ntheir conduct during their diplomatic/consular assignments abroad. \nThe case of the Saudi diplomat is being dealt with accordingly. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S6_U_476": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \nDEPARTMENT OF POSTS  \n \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.476 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 2ND DECEMBER, 2015 \n \nMONEY ORDERS \n \n476.  SHRI S. RAJENDRAN: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \nbe pleased to  state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has received complaints of non -delivery and late \ndelivery of money orders to the recipients and if so, the number of such complaints \nreceived separately, especially in rural areas during the last three years, State/UT-wise; \n \n(b)  the details of inquiry conducted in this regard and the action taken against those \nfound  responsible along with the corrective measures taken to address the complaints  \nand streamline the money order service; and \n \n(c)  whether the Government has introduced/implemented instant money order \nscheme in the post offices across the country and if so, the details thereof along with \nthe benefits accrued as a result thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF COMMUNICATIONS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI RAVI SHANKAR PRASAD) \n \n(a)  Yes Madam. Complaints of non-delivery and late delivery of money orders to the \nrecipients have been received. The number of complaints received regarding non -\ndelivery and late delivery of money orders to the recipients during the last three years is \nas follows: \nA. Non-delivery of Money Orders: \n S. \nNo. \nState/           \nUnion Territory \n2012-13 2013-14 2014-15 \nRural Urban Total Rural Urban Total Rural Urban Total \nStates \n1 Andhra Pradesh 484 627 1111 230 496 826 205 177 382 \n2 Arunachal \nPradesh \nNil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil \n3 Assam 20 55 75 11 51 62 12 49 61 \n \nContd…….2/- \n\n \n-2- \n \n4 Bihar 1198 514 1712 569 244 813 150 65 215 \n5 Chhattisgarh 125 96 221 181 86 267 40 32 72 \n6 Goa 7 3 10 16 4 20 3 1 4 \n7 Gujarat 1546 1714 3260 1285 1465 2750 555 734 1289 \n8 Haryana 496 360 856 