at 633 2381 3014 542 1356 1898 355 759 1114 \n8 Haryana 516 133 649 524 156 680 301 106 407 \n9 Himachal Pradesh 132 42 174 111 39 150 43 12 55 \n10 Jammu & Kashmir 840 214 1054 858 234 1092 426 82 508 \n11 Jharkhand 82 15 97 51 08 59 105 16 121 \n12 Karnataka 449 504 953 443 574 1017 336 523 859 \n13 Kerala 1600 419 2019 612 226 838 281 154 435 \n14 Madhya Pradesh  326 367 693 406 338 744 290 308 598 \n15 Maharashtra 1674 872 2546 1732 502 2032 740 638 1378 \n16 Manipur Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil \n17 Mizoram Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil \n18 Meghalaya 07 05 12 10 05 15 17 14 31 \n19 Nagaland Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil Nil \n20 Odisha 1138 380 1518 919 473 1392 972 292 1264 \n21 Punjab 169 149 318 154 129 283 193 119 312 \n22 Rajasthan 693 642 1335 582 590 1172 817 759 1576 \n23 Sikkim 7 2 9 24 3 27 48 3 51 \nContd………5/- \n\n \n-5- \n24 Tamil Nadu 387 684 1071 377 693 1070 328 398 726 \n25 Telangana       39 115 154 \n26 Tripura 16 01 17 17 Nil 17 10 02 12 \n27 Uttar Pradesh 1123 2726 3849 1083 2068 3151 874 2023 2897 \n28 Uttarakhand 220 154 374 195 127 322 135 95 230 \n29 West Bengal 158 61 219 2668 249 2917 3399 432 3831 \nUnion Territories \n1 Andaman & \nNicobar Islands \n20 1 21 112 0 112 141 2 143 \n2 Chandigarh 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \n3 Dadra & Nagar \nHaveli \n0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \n4 Daman and Diu 1 7 8 2 8 10 2 7 9 \n5 Delhi 662 317 979 484 110 594 210 98 308 \n6 Lakshadweep 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 1 1 \n7 Puducherry 7 11 18 5 12 17 4 14 18 \n Total 14600 12022 26622 13092 8715 21809 10757 7356 18113 \n \n(b) Enquiries are conducted to ascertain the actual reason for non -payment or late \npayment of Money Orders. The cause of delay for payment of money order may be due to \nseveral reasons such as absence of payee/non -availability of payee at the time of delivery, \ndeath of payee, wrong / incomplete address, incorrect PIN Code or change in address, \ntechnical problems in electronic transmission system, delay in transmission of money \norders due to natural calamities, civil disturbance like bandhs, hartals, transport st rike, \nconstraint of intra city movement . Accordingly, cause of action is decided to settle the \ncomplaint. The information regarding number of inquiries conducted in 2012 -13, 2013-14 \nand 2014-15 is at Annexure-I. \nContd……6/- \n\n \n-6- \nIf any official is found at fault in late payment or non -payment of money orders, \nsuitable administrative/disciplinary action is taken depending on gravity of lapses noticed. \nThe information regarding the number of officials against whom administrative/dis ciplinary \naction has been taken in 2012-13, 2013-14 and 2014-15 is at Annexure-II.  \nIn case of non-payment of money order due to service fault, duplicate money orders \nare issued. The Department has introduced electronic transmission of money orders for \ntheir speedy transmission to the office of delivery. Where technological faults in technical \ntransmission are noticed, suitable action for rectification is taken. If there is a problem with \ncash flow, action is taken to improve the cash flow and authorized ba lances of Post Offices \nare revised to meet the cash requirements. Computerized Customer Care Centre (CCC) \nbased Grievance Redress Mechanism is set in place to facilitate efficient handling of \ncomplaints.  \n(c) Yes Madam, the Government has introduced instan t money order service on 20 th \nJanuary 2006. This service is now available in 16983 Post Offices across the country as on \n31.10.2015. The service is instant, convenient, reliable and affordable. The maximum limit \nof remitting money is Rs.50,000/ - whereas for the ordinary money order it is Rs. 5,000/ - \nonly. The tariff charged for this service is also very low as compared to the ordinary money \norder.  \n \n \n \n \n  \nContd…….7/-  \n\n \n-7- \n \nAnnexure I \nNumber of Inquiries Conducted during the last three years \n \nSer \nNo \nName of Circle 2012-13 2013-14 2014-15 Total Remarks \n1. Andhra Pradesh 660 