    "ls|LS16_S6_U_489": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.  489 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON  02.12.2015 \n \nRAILWAY SCHOOLS  \n  \n   489.  SHRI VINOD LAKHAMASHI CHAVDA: \n     \n          Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the total number  of Railway Schools in the country at \npresent; \n \n(b)   whether it is a fact that there is acute sho rtage of \nteachers in Railway Schools in  the country including \nGujarat;  \n \n(c)  if so, the reasons therefor; and \n \n(d)    the action being taken by the Governme nt to fill up   \n   the vacant posts at  the earliest? \n  \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n ( SHRI MANOJ SINHA ) \n \n(a): Indian Railways is running 150 Railway schools in the \ncountry.  \n(b) to (d):  Certain vacancies of teachers  do exist in Railway \nschools. However, occurrence of vacancies is a natural and \ncontinuous p rocess for which indents are placed on the \nRailway Recruitment Boards by the concerned Zonal Railways \nand recruitments also take place. \n****** ",
    "ls|LS16_S6_U_490": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 490 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON DECEMBER 02, 2015 \n \nTASK FORCE ON POVERTY ALLEVIATION \n \nNo. 490 COL. SONARAM CHOUDHARY:   \n   \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AN D URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \nbe pleased to state:- \n(a) the features of poverty alleviation policy in the country;  \n(b) whether the State of Ra jasthan has set up a task force in this \nregard, if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether this task force has submitted any suggestions to NITI \nAayog, if so, the details thereof; and \n(d) whether the Government proposes  to take Special steps and \nmake budgetary provisions for pove rty alleviation in the poor \nand backward area of Rajasthan, if so, the details thereof and \nif not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN  \nTHE MINISTRY OF HOUSING & URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \n[SHRI BABUL SUPRIYO] \n**** \n(a) :This Ministry has been im plementing National Urban \nLivelihood Mission (NULM) with  the objective of reducing \npoverty and vulnerability of urban poor households.  The \nMission envisages universal Soci al Mobilization of urban poor \ninto Self-Help Groups (SHGs) and their federations.  It has a \nprovision for skill training of urban poor to increase their \nincome through structured, ma rket-oriented ce rtified courses \nthat can provide sala ried employment and/ or self-employment \nopportunities.  It also focus es on financial assistance to \nindividuals/groups/SHGs of ur ban poor for setting up gainful \nself-employment ventures.  Unde r the Mission, for the urban \nhomeless population permanent shelters equipped with basic \nContd.Pg..2/- \n \n\n-2- \namenities are also constructed.   It also addresses the \nlivelihood concerns of the urban street vendors by facilitating \nsurvey, issue of certificate and creation of infrastructure \nfacilities.  \n(b) :The State Government of Raja sthan has set up a Task Force \non Elimination of Poverty  on 01.05.201 5 under the \nChairpersonship of Chief Secretary, Govt. of Rajasthan. \n \n(c) :The Government of Rajasthan has submitted the Report of the \nTask Force dated 15.06.2015 to NITI Aayog. \n \n(d) :During 2014-15 Rs. 42.01 Crore were released under NULM to \nRajasthan . In 2015-16 Rs.62.99 Crores have been allocated for \nthe state.  \n \n****** \n \n  \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S6_U_491": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.491 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2015 \n \nGUIDELINES FOR RECEIVING GIFTS \n \n†491.  SHRI ALOK SANJAR: \n  \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether guidelines have been prescribed by the Government \nregarding receiving gifts by the Very Important Persons in \nother countries; \n \n(b)   if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c)  whether such gifts received by the individual becomes his \npersonal property; \n \n(d)   if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(e)  the year -wise and country -wise details of gifts rece ived \nabroad by VVIPs during the last three years? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) & (b)  Yes. The gifts received by Very Important Persons \nduring their foreign visits are governed by Foreign Contribution \n(Acceptance or Retention of Gifts or Presentations) Rules, 2012 as \namended from time to time.  \n \n(c) & (d)  The ownership of the gifts are decided  as per the \ncriteria as laid down in Foreign Contribution (Acceptance or \nRetention of Gifts or Presentations) Rules, 2012. \n \n(e) The year-wise and country -wise details of gifts received from \nforeign source by VVIPs during the last three years are enclosed at \nANNEXURE. \n***** \n\nANNEXURE \nYear wise and Country wise details of gifts received by VVIPs during last 3 year  \n \nSl.No Name of Country  2013 2014 2015 till date  \n1 Uzbekistan  1 Nil  3 \n2 Afghanistan 4 2 3 \n3 Kuwait 9 Nil Nil \n4 Peru 1 Nil Nil \n5 Ecuador  1 Nil Nil \n6  Zanzibar Nil 2 Nil \n7 Bahrain Nil 1 Nil \n8 Saudi Arabia  Nil 3 Nil \n9 Myanmar Nil 3 3 \n10 China 3 8 22 \n11 Bangladesh 1 6 19 \n12 United States of America 5 1 7 \n13 Lao PDR Nil Nil 1 \n14 Cambodia  Nil Nil 2 \n15 Indonesia 1 1 2 \n16 Nepal 1 7 5 \n17 United Kingdom 1 1 8 \n18 Bhutan  1 3 1 \n19 South Africa 1 Nil 2 \n20 ASEAN 1 Nil Nil \n21 Cote D'Ivoire 1 Nil  Nil \n22 Germany  2 1 2 \n23 Maldives 2 5 3 \n24 Thailand 2 1 1 \n25 Japan 5 2 3 \n26 Malaysia 3 1 Nil \n27 Fiji 1 Nil 3 \n28 Sri Lanka  2 1 6 \n29 Rome 1 Nil  Nil \n30 Iraq 1 Nil Nil \n31 Vietnam 2 Nil 2 \n32 Pakistan 2 Nil Nil \n33 Russia 3 5 7 \n34 Mexico  1 Nil Nil \n35 Hungary  1 Nil Nil \n36 Niue 1 Nil Nil \n37 Oman Nil 3 Nil \n38 Nigeria  Nil 2 1 \n39 Tanzania  Nil 1 1 \n\n40 Hague, Netherlands Nil 1 1 \n41 Brazil Nil 2 1 \n42 Singapore 1 2 3 \n43 Uganda  Nil 1 Nil \n44 Guyana Nil Nil 2 \n45 Australia Nil Nil 4 \n46 United Nations Nil Nil 2 \n47 Israel Nil Nil 2 \n48 Qatar Nil Nil 2 \n49 Cuba Nil Nil 1 \n50 France Nil Nil 3 \n51 Canada Nil Nil 3 \n52 Spain Nil Nil 1 \n53 Korea Nil Nil 2 \n54 South Korea Nil Nil 9 \n55 Mongolia Nil Nil 4 \n56 Turkmenistan Nil Nil 3 \n57 Tajikistan Nil Nil 2 \n58 Kazakhstan Nil Nil 2 \n59 Mozambique Nil Nil 1 \n60 Micronesia Nil Nil 1 \n61 Marshall Island Nil Nil 1 \n62  Seychelles Nil Nil 3 \n63 Iran Nil Nil 1 \n64 UAE Nil Nil 1 \n65 Kyrgyzstan Nil Nil 1 \n66 Vanuatu Nil Nil 1 \n67 Ireland Nil Nil 1 \n68 Morocco Nil Nil 3 \n69 Namibia Nil Nil 1 \n70 Ghana Nil Nil 1 \n71 Botswana Nil Nil 1 \n72 Mauritius Nil Nil 1 \n73 Senegal Nil Nil 1 \n74 Sierra Leone Nil Nil 1 \n75 Zambia Nil Nil 1 \n76 Madagascar Nil Nil 1 \n77 Liberia Nil Nil 1 \n78 Zimbabwe Nil Nil 1 \n79 Benin Nil Nil 1 \n80 Swaziland Nil Nil 1 \n81 Sudan Nil Nil 1 \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S6_U_492": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 492 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON DECEMBER 2, 2015 \nE-GAZETTE NOTIFICATION \n \n No. 492 SHRI VIJAY KUMAR HANSDAK: \nWill the Minister of URBAN DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n(a) whether his Ministry proposes to issue e-gazette notification to \ntake forward the Digital India Campaign; \n(b) if so, the details thereof and its likely benefits;  \n(c) whether the e-gazette  notification will hav e validity in all \nGovernment Departments under IT Act, 2000; and \n(d) if so, the current status of the pr oposal and the time by which it \nis likely to be completed ? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN \nDEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI BABUL SUPRIYO) \n(a) & (b): Yes, Madam.  Ministry of Urban Development has issued a \nnotification No. O-17022/ 1/2015-PSP-1, dat ed 30/09/2015, to \npublish e-gazette notifications  by way of uploading and \npublishing on the official websit e.  This has been implemented \nwith effect from 01 st October, 2015, and physical printing of \ngazette notifications by the Go vernment of India presses has \nbeen discontinued.  The benefit s of e-publishi ng include ease \nand immediate access to e-publis hed gazette notifications by \nany citizen.  It has also reduced the delays in publishing gazette \nnotifications as well as will resu lt in environmental benefits due \nto discontinuation of physical printing.  \n \n(c): The e-gazette notifications ar e applicable to all Government of \nIndia gazette publications and will be valid for all Government of \nIndia gazettes.  \n(d): The e-publishing of gazettes  and discontinuat ion of physical \nprinting has already been implemented since 01st October,2015 \n****** ",
    "ls|LS16_S6_U_493": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 493 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2015 \n \nAUTOMATIC DOORS IN COACHES \n \n493.  SHRI MULLAPPALLY RAMACHANDRAN: \n \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether Railways has decided to install automatic doors in \ncoaches of trains; and  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the action plan chalked out for the \nsame?  \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n (SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n(a) & (b) : Yes, Madam.  Integral Coach Factory (ICF), Chennai has \nprovided Automatic Sliding Doors on 13 Metro Rakes (8 Car Formation) \nwhich are currently running in Kolkata Metro. Besides, ICF is currently \nproviding Automatic Sliding Doors on fully Air -conditioned (AC) Electric \nMultiple Unit (EMU) Train Set for Mumbai Suburban. Similarly, Rail Coach \nFactory (RCF), Kapurthala has developed design for semi -high speed \nLinke Hofmann Busch  (LHB) rake having high speed potential of 200 \nkmph with Automatic doors.  \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S6_U_494": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nDEPARTMENT OF ATOMIC ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.494 \n TO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2015 \n \nKUDANKULAM NPP-II \n \n494.  SHRI P. KUMAR: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Kudankulam Nuclear Power Plant Uni t-II is yet to be \n commissioned/yet to produce power; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the reasons the refor; and \n \n(c)  the steps taken by the Government to expedite operationalizing this unit and \n ensure all safety parameters are put in place? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVAN CES & \nPENSIONS AND PRIME MINISTER’S OFFICE (Dr. JITENDRA SINGH) :     \n \n(a)  Yes, Sir; \n(b)  The hot run which is a pre-requisite for downs tream activities like fuel loading \nand approach to first criticality, has been success fully completed in \naccordance with laid down procedures and regulatory  requirements. The unit \nis being prepared for further activities and commissioning of unit-II is expected \nin the first quarter of 2016-17.   \n(c)  Close monitoring is being carried out to exped ite the commissioning activities. \n In order to ensure safety, apart from the checks a nd the tests conducted by \n the operator, a detailed review at every step is d one by the Atomic Energy \n Regulatory Board (AERB) before accord of clearance  for the next step.  \n \n*****  ",
    "ls|LS16_S6_U_495": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVANCES AND PENSIONS \n(DEPARTMENT OF PERSONNEL AND TRAINING) \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 495 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2015) \n \nINVESTIGATION OF EMPLOYEES \n \n495. SHRI OM BIRLA: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has hired retired Government servants with clean record to \ninvestigate cases against current Government servants and if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(b)  whether the Government has finalised the selection process of such a panel and if so, \nthe details thereof; and \n \n(c)  the number of pending cases against current officials proposed to be investigated? \n \nANSWER \n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions and Minister \nof State in the Prime Minister’s Office. (DR. JITENDRA SINGH) \n(a) to (c):    The Government is in the process of laying down the procedure for empanelment \nof retired officers as the Inquiry Officers for conducting Departmental Inquiries  by the Cadre \nControlling Authorities. \n \n The services of the Inquiry Officers could be utilized by the Ministries/Departments \nand their subordinate offices/organizations under the Gov ernment of India for conducting \ndepartmental inquiries against the delinquent officials, as and when the procedure is finalized. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S6_U_496": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 496 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, THE 2ND DECEMBER, 2015 \n \nSURVEY OF NSSO \n \n496. SHRI SHIVKUMAR UDASI: \n \nWill the Minister of STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) the average per capita monthly expenditure of rural and urban \npopulation as per the recent survey of the National Sample Survey \nOrganisation (NSSO); \n(b) whether as per recent survey of NSSO, there has been a \ncontinuous decline in spending on food in rural areas; and \n(c) if so, the percentage of spending on food out of the total \nexpenditure during each of the last three years  and the current  \nyear and the steps taken by the Government in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEP ENDENT CHARGE) FOR MINISTRY OF \nSTATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION,  MINISTER OF STATE \nFOR MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS AND MINISTER OF STATE FOR \nMINISTRY OF OVERSEAS INDIAN AFFAIRS [ GENERAL ( Dr.) V.K. SINGH  \n(Retd.)] \n \n(a): As per the recent survey of National Sample Survey Office (NSSO) on \nHousehold Consumer Expenditure conducted during July 2011 to June \n2012, the average Monthly Per Capita Expenditure  using Uniform \nReference Period (URP) was estimated as Rs.1279 in rural India and         \nRs. 2399 in urban India. \n \n\n(b): No, Madam. The details of estimated Average Monthly Per Capita \nConsumer Expenditure on Food Items in rural areas using Uniform \nReference Period are as under: \n \nPeriod In Rs. \n2004-05 307.60 \n2009-10 497.09 \n2011-12 621.96 \n \n(c): Does not arise. \n  \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S6_U_497": " \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 497 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, DECEMBER 02, 2015 \n \nEARTHQUAKE WARNING \n \n497.  SHRI JAYADEV GALLA: \n \n        Will the Minister of EARTH SCIENCES be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether Indian Institute of Technology, Roorkee, is working on a pilot \nproject 'Earthquake Early Warning System which gives early warning \nabout earthquake; and \n(b)   if so, the details of the project? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY AND \nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES  \n(SHRI Y. S. CHOWDARY) \n(a-b)  Yes Madam. Under the project, installed network of 100 sensors in a \nsmall area of 70x60km in central Himalayan region is expected to \ndetect the initial ground motion from an earthquake rupture and \nestimate the resulting ground shaking expected later in time either at \nsame location or  at some other location s. The emerging warning time \nexpected may range from few seconds to a little more than 60 seconds \nand will primarily be a function of the distance from the epicenter in \nHimalayan region. \n \n \n \n****** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S6_U_498": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(DEPARTMENT OF ELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY) \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 498 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 02.12.2015 \n \n \nCYBER SAFETY \n \n498 SHRI BHAGWANTH  KHUBA: \n                    \n Will the Minister of Communications & Information Technology be pleased to state: - \n \n(a) whether  the Government is planning to frame cyber safety policy; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) the timeframe for introduction of such policy? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER FOR COMMUNICATIONS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY   \n(SHRI RAVI SHANKAR PRASAD) \n \n (a), (b) and  (c): At present, there is no proposal before the Government to frame a \nseparate cyber safety policy, as the National Cyber Security Policy published by the \nGovernment on 2 nd July 2013 articulates a clear vision to build and promote a safe, \nsecure and resilient  cyber space for citizens, businesses and Government. This policy \ncontains specific provisions aimed at creating awareness among the users with regard to \nsafe and secure use of cyber space. \n \n*********  \n\n ",
    "ls|LS16_S6_U_499": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.499  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2015 \n \nRAIL COACH FACTORIES IN INDIA \n \n499.  DR. K. KAMARAJ:   \n            \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the number of Rail Coach Factories in India; \n \n(b) the type and the number of coaches produced during the past  \nthree years; \n \n(c) the number of coaches allotted to each railway region; and \n \n(d) whether Railways is proposing to establish electric multiple  units \nor diesel electric multiple units coach factory in Tamil Nadu and if \nso, the details thereof? \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n( SHRI MANOJ SINHA ) \n \n \n(a) to (d)   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n***** \n\nSTATEMENT  REFERRED  TO  IN  REPLY  TO  PARTS   (a)  TO  (d)  OF  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.  499  BY  DR. K. KAMARAJ  TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 02.12.2015 REGARDING RAIL COACH \nFACTORIES IN INDIA. \n \n(a) At present, there are three Rail Coach Factories under Ministry of \nRailways.  In addition, a new DEMU factor y at Haldia in West Bengal \nhas recently started furnishing of Diesel Electric Multiple Units \n(DEMU). \n \n(b) Type and number of coaches produced for Indian Railways by these \nfactories during the past three years are given below: \n \n 2012-13 2013-14 2014-15 \nSelf Propelled coaches   607   253   329 \nLHB design coaches   560   543   555 \nICF design coaches 2105 2493 2430 \nTotal 3272 3289 3314 \n \n(c) Allotment of coaches to Zonal Railways varies from time to time \naccording to their requirement and is an on -going pro cess. After \nallotment of coaches, these could be diverted for the use of other \nzones as per requirement.  However, the initial zone-wise allotments of \ncoaches during the current financial year is as under:- \n \nZone Number of coaches allotted \n(April 2015 to Oct 2015) \nCentral 330 \nEastern 248 \n\nEast Central 128 \nEast Coast 106 \nNorthern 328 \nNorth Central 65 \nNorth Eastern 138 \nNorth East Frontier 275 \nNorth Western 58 \nSouthern 148 \nSouth Central 209 \nSouth Eastern 124 \nSouth East Central 78 \nSouth Western 89 \nWestern 180 \nWest Central  92 \nKonkan Railway 14 \nTotal 2610 \n \n(d) At present, there is no proposal to set up any Electric Multiple Unit or \nDiesel Electric Multiple Unit coach factory in Tamil Nadu.  Integral \nCoach Factory at Chennai in Tamil Nadu is alre ady manufacturing \nvarious types of coaches which includes Electric Multiple Units and \nDiesel Electric Multiple Units. \n \n***** \n \n                         \n "
  }
}